    "final_answer": "I found the answer. The character at Unicode 8902 (decimal) is the \"STAR OPERATOR\" (⋆), which has a 6-pointed star shape that resembles a snowflake.\n\n## Answer\n\n**Unicode character 8902** (which corresponds to U+22C6 in hexadecimal) is the character that looks like a snowflake. Its name is **\"STAR OPERATOR\"** (⋆), and it has a distinctive 6-pointed asterisk-like shape that resembles a snowflake.\n\nWolfram Alpha's image visualization clearly showed this character among the range 8900-8920 (decimal), and clicking on character 8902 confirmed it. The character is also grouped with similar star-like characters (Arabic five pointed star, black star, white medium star) which reinforces its snowflake-like appearance.",
